**This is a Full time opportunity for candidates based in Eastern Europe/Israel**

The UserWay Project Manager will spearhead the iterative approach to delivering a project throughout its life cycle. As PM, you will lead a cross functional development team through all phases of the product ownership, development process, from discovery, through development, to product launch. The role entails team management, planning, customer interactions, and process management. At the core, projects handled by the agile PM should exhibit central values and behaviors of trust, flexibility, empowerment and collaboration.

Responsibilities:

- Validate the Scrum Maturity of the team and coach the team to higher levels of maturity, at an ambitious yet sustainable pace for the team and organization (guiding the team on how to use Agile/Scrum practices and values);
- Product ownership and project management;
- Assist in team development by removing road-blocks, mentoring members and efficient utilization of organizational resources to improve capacity;
- Work with QA Manager and testing team to ensure thorough testing of modules/application/interfaces;
- Compile historical data available with the team and present it for reference of senior officials and the team members on the project;
- Train team members on agile methodologies;
- Present weekly status reports to senior management.

Requirements:
- 3-5 years relevant PM experience with SaaS and/or web products;
- Relevant product management or project management experience;
- Must have Bachelor's degree or higher in Computer Science, Business, Engineering, Project Management, Information Technology, Management, Technical, Information Systems or other relevant degrees;
- Impeccable English communication skills;
- Must have one or more valid Agile PM License or Certifications (e.g., PMP, CSM, APMI, CSPO, SCRUM, ACP, CSP, CEC, ITIL, PRINCE2, PMI, etc.);
- Must have experience in maintaining software systems (Saas, Web, etc.);
- Ability to work under pressure in a fast paced and rigorous environment.

